This is a community project. It is not an official LiveKit SDK and is not
affiliated with or endorsed by LiveKit, Inc.

This product is designed after the LiveKit Agents frameworks:

  - livekit/agents (Python), Copyright LiveKit, Inc., Apache License 2.0
    https://github.com/livekit/agents
  - livekit/agents-js (TypeScript), Copyright LiveKit, Inc., Apache License 2.0
    https://github.com/livekit/agents-js

No source code from those projects is included. The worker protocol flow,
default values (for example endpointing and interruption delays, the job
assignment timeout, the reconnection schedule) and wire-level names
(participant attributes such as "lk.agent.state" and "lk.agent.name", the
"lk.transcription" topic) follow their behaviour so that agents built with
this SDK interoperate with LiveKit servers and clients.

This product depends on, and links against, the following LiveKit modules,
each licensed under the Apache License 2.0, Copyright LiveKit, Inc.:

  - github.com/livekit/server-sdk-go
  - github.com/livekit/protocol
  - github.com/livekit/media-sdk

Other notable dependencies: github.com/pion/webrtc (MIT),
github.com/gorilla/websocket (BSD-2-Clause), google.golang.org/protobuf
(BSD-3-Clause), gopkg.in/hraban/opus.v2 (MIT). The room audio path links
against the native libraries libopus and libopusfile (BSD-3-Clause) and
libsoxr (LGPL-2.1-or-later, dynamically linked).

The package vad/silero embeds the Silero VAD model, release 6.2.3
